WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.650
An old king gives away his kingdom, and
hands over his coronet to be shared.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.500
But he keeps "The name, and
all the addition to a king".

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.100
The title, without the work.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.930
Two acts later, he stands
bareheaded in a storm.

5
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.810
From the throne to a beggar in the rain.

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.460
Did it teach him anything,
or does he just suffer?

7
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:26.350
In this mission, you'll read
what he says out in that storm:

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.110
"Poor naked wretches, wheresoe’er
you are," You'll trace his fall,

9
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.290
stage by stage, down to
an old man on his knees.

10
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.520
And you'll weigh what all
that suffering adds up to.

11
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.600
Your mission: decide whether Lear learns,

12
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:42.950
or only suffers.
